\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every closed connected symplectic manifold M and every Hamiltonian diffeomorphism $\varphi $ with nondegenerate fixed points, must $\#Fix(\varphi )$ be at least the minimum number of critical points of a Morse function on M? The minimum is restricted to Morse functions, whereas the existing Crit record is not.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every closed connected symplectic manifold M and every Hamiltonian diffeomorphism $\varphi $ with nondegenerate fixed points, must $\#Fix(\varphi )$ be at least the minimum number of critical points of a Morse function on M? The minimum is restricted to Morse functions, whereas the existing Crit record is not.

